-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Runtime dependency: mpc2emu
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VinSamLib deliberately never edits mpc2emu — it is used as a separate,
external runtime dependency (a sibling checkout, its path configured in
Settings), never vendored or copied into this repository. Every E4B/KRZ/
EIII *bank writer* and every DSP routine this app exposes (vintage
resample profiles, key-zone/velocity-layer reduction, XPM parsing) is
mpc2emu's own code, invoked through vinsamlib/mpc2emu_bridge.py's lazy
module proxies.

  mpc2emu — Multi-format Sampler Converter
  https://github.com/ (see the mpc2emu project's own README/LICENSE)
  License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)

mpc2emu's own LICENSE file carries its full, detailed third-party credit
chain (emu3fs, emu3bm, KurzFiler, ConvertWithMoss, libgig, and others it
draws on for the formats it reads/writes) — see that project directly
rather than this file duplicating it, since VinSamLib does not touch
that code and cannot vouch for it beyond mpc2emu's own statements.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party references and their licenses (VinSamLib's own code)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vinsamlib/vfs/emu3.py
  The EMU3 filesystem read-side logic (superblock geometry, FAT,
  directory layout, cluster allocation) mirrors the parsing already
  proven in mpc2emu's own writers/iso_builder.py (emu_hdd_append), which
  is itself derived from:
    emu3fs — Copyright (C) David García Goñi
    https://github.com/dagargo/emu3fs
    License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  No source code was copied from emu3fs or from mpc2emu; this is an
  independent reimplementation of the read path informed by that prior
  reverse-engineering work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

vinsamlib/vfs/fatvol.py, vinsamlib/vfs/iso9660.py
  FAT12/16/32 and ISO 9660 are public, vendor-neutral format
  specifications; these readers are original implementations against
  those public specifications, not derived from any third-party source.
  Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

vinsamlib/banks/e4b.py, vinsamlib/banks/krz.py
  Original, container-level (byte-verbatim) readers for the E4B and KRZ
  bank formats, informed by mpc2emu's own documented format references
  (docs/E4B_FORMAT.md, docs/KRZ_FORMAT.md in the mpc2emu repository).
  No source code was copied. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

vinsamlib/banks/eiii.py
  Original, container-level (byte-verbatim) reader/assembler for the
  E-mu Emulator IIIX/ESI-32 (`.e3x`/`.esi`, plus read-only `.e3b`
  Emulator III) bank formats, informed by mpc2emu's own documented
  format reference (docs/EIII_FORMAT.md) and writer
  (writers/eiii_writer.py) in the mpc2emu repository -- no reference
  implementation for this format existed anywhere prior to mpc2emu's
  own from-scratch reverse-engineering effort. No source code was
  copied. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

All other files
  Original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

